ht=\"300\" srcset=\"https:\/\/washvoiceafrica.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/Elizabeth-2023-268x300.jpeg 268w, https:\/\/washvoiceafrica.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/08\/Elizabeth-2023.jpeg 562w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 268px) 100vw, 268px\" \/><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-33 elementor-inner-column elementor-element elementor-element-63bcdcfc\" data-id=\"63bcdcfc\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-2ae97f5 wow fadeInRight elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"2ae97f5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">WaSHVoice founding CEO and Program Director:<\/span><\/h3><p><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> She is a recognized Water and Sanitation professional responsible for strategic decisions for WaSHVoice.<\/span><\/i><\/p><p><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Elizabeth developed her skills in water and sanitation sector through hands-on experience, peer to peer learning, sector knowledge management among others activities. Established and served as the first Corporate planning and monitoring department head for Nairobi City Water and Sewerage Company, worked as organizing committee member for many national and international conferences.\u00a0<\/span><\/i><i><\/i><i style=\"font-family: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;\">A graduate of Sanitation Global Graduate School IHE Delft Water institute, she is passionate about proper WaSH management through appropriate policies and standards.<\/i><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-column elementor-col-33 elementor-inner-column elementor-element elementor-element-ddbe4b8\" data-id=\"ddbe4b8\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-570d64a wow fadeInRight elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"570d64a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><i style=\"font-family: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;\">\u00a0<\/i><i style=\"font-family: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;\">She designed and founded the Women in Water and Sanitation Association (WIWAS).\u00a0<\/i><i style=\"font-family: inherit; font-weight: inherit; letter-spacing: 0px;\">She also served as Secretary General, partners liaison, and fund raising director. She is a recognized\u00a0 pioneer member of Africa Water Association (AFWA) professional women caucus. Actively participated in nature conservancy and green campaigns for water and sanitation. Dynamically contributed to water service provider\u2019s association in developing strategic plans. Participated in development of Kenya water sector improvement plan in various capacities among many notable achievements.<\/i><\/p><p><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Elizabeth holds an Msc Degree in Sanitation from IHE Delft Institute of Water Education, BA in sociology and economics, and a Diploma in Surveying and Mapping.\u00a0 She has several certificates in water and sanitation planning, and management.<\/span><\/i><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"has_eae_slider elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-ff1739f elementor-section-full_width elementor-section-height-default eleme